{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The&nbsp;proposed development fails to provide sufficient information with respect to the provision and management of car parking and waste management and storage and the provision of secure cycle parking.&nbsp; The proposal is therefore likely to result in a detrimental impact on the site and surrounding area with inadequate bin storage proposed and insufficient information provided regarding the management of waste. It is therefore contrary to the following: - The National Planning Policy Framework&nbsp;(NPPF) (MHCLG, 2024)-&nbsp;Policies DMT 2, DMT 3, DMS1 and DMSI 8 of&nbsp;The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan 2037&nbsp;(September 2024)",
    "&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;1.&amp;nbsp;The proposal&amp;nbsp;fails to demonstrate it would&amp;nbsp;be located within an appropriate location and would result in the further intensification of the rear amenity area of the existing commercial site. On this basis the application is&amp;nbsp;contrary to:&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;- The National Planning Policy Framework National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024)&lt;br&gt;-&amp;nbsp;Policies&amp;nbsp;D1, D4,&amp;nbsp; and D5 of the London Plan (March 2021)&lt;br&gt;-&amp;nbsp;Policies DMD1, DMD6, DME3, SP5, and DME3 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham Local Plan 2037 (September, 2024)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
